=== ORCH-055 fix: driveSite() no longer calls setCancelToken() unconditionally, orchestrator-executed 2026-09-05 ===

Defect (ORCH-055): fixture::driveSite()'s 4th parameter was `CancelToken cancelToken =
CancelToken()`, and the callee called `service->setCancelToken(cancelToken)` UNCONDITIONALLY,
whether the caller supplied an argument or fell through to the default. T-148's
guiThread_defaultTokenNeverCancels() rows therefore never left CloudService::cancelToken_ at its
own construction-time default -- they overwrote it with a freshly-constructed CancelToken() every
row, which is behaviourally identical to a correct member default ONLY if that default is itself
correct. A broken member initializer for cancelToken_ would have been silently papered over.

Fix (unittests/Core/garminconnect/testCloudProviderWatchdog.cpp):
  - #include <optional> added.
  - driveSite()'s 4th parameter changed from `CancelToken cancelToken = CancelToken()` to
    `std::optional<CancelToken> cancelToken = std::nullopt`.
  - Body changed from unconditional `service->setCancelToken(cancelToken);` to
    `if (cancelToken) service->setCancelToken(*cancelToken);` -- "no token supplied" now
    genuinely skips the setter call.
  - The one explicit-token caller (shapeBC_cancellationBreaksTheListing,
    `driveSite(id, plans, 5000, CancelToken(flag))`) needed NO change: std::optional converts
    implicitly from its value type.
  - guiThread_defaultTokenNeverCancels()'s own comment updated to state it now exercises
    CloudService's own default, not a substitute.

